      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n&amp; \\text{Choose the first digit, there are $4$ choices: $1$, $3$, $5$, $7$, $9$.} \\\\\n&amp; \\text{Choose the second digit, after selecting the first one, $9$ possibilities remain.} \\\\\n&amp; \\text{Choose the third digit, $8$ possibilities remain.} \\\\\n&amp; \\text{The total number of odd numbers between $100$ and $999$ is $4\\times9\\times8 = 288$;} \\\\\n&amp; \\text{Show the average number of digits of the odd numbers is $3$, which is also odd.} \\\\\n&amp; \\text{Therefore, these $288$ odd numbers between $100$ and $999$ have odd numbers of digits.}\n\\end{align*}\nHence, there are $\\boxed{288}$ odd numbers between $100$ and $999$ that have distinct digits.",
